## Mapping from the DatoCMS UI

The tables below map every field of the "Create a new webhook" form in the DatoCMS UI (Settings > Webhooks) to its Terraform attribute. Fields marked with `*` are required in the UI. The "Default" column shows the value this provider (and the UI form) uses when the attribute is omitted.

### General

| UI field | Terraform attribute | Default |
|---|---|---|
| Name* | `name` | required |
| Enabled? (toggle) | `enabled` | `true` |
| Automatic retries? (toggle; the UI notes delivery is retried up to 7 times on timeouts or errors) | `auto_retry` | `false` |

### Triggers

| UI field | Terraform attribute | Default |
|---|---|---|
| Add new trigger | `events` (each trigger is one list element with `entity_type`, `event_types` and optional `filters`) | required, at least one |

### HTTP Settings

| UI field | Terraform attribute | Default |
|---|---|---|
| URL* | `url` | required |
| HTTP basic auth > User | `http_basic_user` | null |
| HTTP basic auth > Password | `http_basic_password` | null |
| Custom headers > Add new header | `headers` | `{}` |

### HTTP Body

| UI field | Terraform attribute | Default |
|---|---|---|
| Payload format* (select) | `payload_api_version` (`"3"` corresponds to the "API Version 3" option) | `"3"` |
| Expand nested blocks in records? (toggle) | `nested_items_in_payload` | `false` |
| Send a custom payload? (toggle plus textarea) | `custom_payload` (setting the attribute equals turning the toggle on; omitting it or null means off) | null |

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Import

Import is supported using the webhook ID, optionally prefixed with the project key of the provider's `api_tokens` map (`project/id`):

{{ codefile "shell" .ImportFile }}

Note: the DatoCMS API returns `http_basic_user` and `http_basic_password` on GET, so the import also populates the basic auth credentials (both attributes are marked sensitive).
